(;FF[4]CA[UTF-8]GM[1]AP[ogs-puzzle-exporter:1.0]GN[4-4 enclosure Submarine Invasion]SZ[19]AB[dd][fc]PL[W];W[bd](;B[cd];W[be];B[bc];W[bb]C[Black will either answer at B5, allowing White to connect under at a in the endgame, or at a, giving White some aji in the corner. ];B[cc];W[ch]LB[ac:A]C[CORRECT])(;B[cc]C[White has not much to do in the corner, and extends along the left side. ];W[cg]C[CORRECT])(;B[bf]C[With B1, Black tries to confine White to the corner. ];W[cc];B[dc];W[bb];B[cf];W[db]C[CORRECT];B[eb]LB[da:A]C[After B7, White usually plays elsewhere. So a is left as a very large point for both sides - note that when Black plays a, the best White can get in this corner is a ko. ]))